{"name":"Nipple","hex":"#bb7777","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nipple","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The projection of a mammary gland from which, on female therian mammals, milk is secreted. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The nipple (noun sense 1) and the areola together."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fit (a baby's bottle, etc.) with a nipple.","To give one's nipple to (a baby) to allow breastfeeding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nipple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nipple","blocks":[{"text":"The nipple is a raised region of tissue on the surface of the breast from which, in lactating females, milk from the mammary gland leaves the body through the lactiferous ducts to nurse an infant. The milk can flow through the nipple passively, or it can be ejected by smooth muscle contractions that occur along with the ductal system. The nipple is surrounded by the areola, which is often a darker colour than the surrounding skin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Closeup_of_female_breast.jpg/330px-Closeup_of_female_breast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nipple","wikidata":"Q188641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png/500px-Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png/1280px-Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png/500px-Breast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The breast: cross-section scheme of the mammary gland: Chest wallPectoralis musclesLobulesNippleAreolaMilk ductFatty tissueSkin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreast_anatomy_normal_scheme.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Nipple_of_male_human.jpg/500px-Nipple_of_male_human.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Nipple_of_male_human.jpg/1280px-Nipple_of_male_human.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Nipple_of_male_human.jpg/500px-Nipple_of_male_human.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nipple of a human male","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANipple_of_male_human.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Breastfeeding_infant.jpg/330px-Breastfeeding_infant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Breastfeeding_infant.jpg/330px-Breastfeeding_infant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Infant latched on to a nipple to breastfeed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreastfeeding_infant.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG/500px-Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG/1280px-Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG/500px-Smoczek_od_butelki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silicone teat, or nipple, used for bottle feeding ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS